# human_body.jp — baseline JavaPowder transform for ALL body-slot cosmetics (cape, wings, etc).
#
# Deliberately EMPTY of position/orientation ops. The decode (floamy/cosmetic_decode.glsl) already
# applies the PIX (JEM->CEM) bridge to every box unconditionally — confirmed by refcape decoding to
# the EXACT reference box values (pos/size/R) with this file empty. The old rotatesc x90/y180/z180 +
# flipface/switchface set here (Y<->Z-conjugated era) fought that and is REMOVED — do not re-add
# without re-validating against a reference decode; it will double-transform.
#
# Per-cosmetic animation (wing flap, cape sway, etc) does NOT belong here — it applies to every body
# cosmetic uniformly. Put it in that cosmetic's OWN cosmetics/<id>/model.jp via `match <id>:*`.
#
# Reference: MagicShaders' CEM_WINGS (assets/minecraft/shaders/include/mods/cem/clasic.glsl:121-155):
#   ADD_BOX_WITH_ROTATION_ROTATE(vec3(-4,3.75,-5), vec3(4,8,0),
#       Rotate3(animationTime * PI * -0.05, Y) * PIX, ...)          # left wing
#   animationTime = cos(GameTime*1000) * (cem_color.g * def_speed) + 22.5     # def_speed = 0.22/120
#   (right wing: pos.x=+4, angle sign flips to `* 0.05`, offset -157.5)
# Ported to JavaPowder as a per-cosmetic `animate` op (see cosmetics/wings/model.jp for the live one):
#   match wings:*
#   animate rot y radians(cos(gametime*1000.0) * 10.0)
# `cem_color.g` (a per-armor tint channel controlling flap speed in the reference) has no cosmetic
# equivalent yet — the ported formula uses a fixed amplitude/speed instead.

match *:*body*
